  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Small and medium-sized enterprises# capacity-building towards the establishment of the industrial innovation hub in Armenia (Phase I)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Following the first National Coordination Body (NCB) meeting for the Country Programme (CP) for inclusive and sustainable industrial development in Armenia 2022-2026 held on 6 June 2022, the delegations of UNIDO and Armenia agreed to organize working-level follow-up consultations between UNIDO technical experts and national focal points from respective line Ministries to identify concrete project proposals to be developed and identify potential resource mobilization opportunities. In 2023 and 2024, following the missions to Yerevan, UNIDO held additional technical consultations with representatives of the Ministry of Economy of Armenia, presenting a technical assistance intervention aimed at reinforcing the key national ICT, innovation, and entrepreneurial ecosystems to support the Strategic Plan for the Development of the Digital Economy in Armenia.  The Ministry of Economy of Armenia requested UNIDO#s assistance to address pressing challenges in SMEs digitalization and industrial innovation.  The present project document was elaborated taking into account national development priorities and specific needs of the Government of Armenia in fulfilling strategic tasks providing a concrete step-by-step intervention that would allow policymakers, ecosystem support institutions, SMEs active in ICT/innovation and ongo</narrative>
  </description>
